From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Publish motion UV with required integer half storage on GLES fallback

Preserve RG16F shaders and filtering on capable contexts. Gate float UV allocation
with GLES core/extension capability and an actual mixed-MRT probe. Otherwise use
required RG16UI storage with half words, typed clearing and decode-before-bilinear
consumers. Keep real fragment output/discard, primary color, dither, once-only
geometry/replay and per-preset previous-field lifecycle. No new render exceptions
or per-frame capability polling. OpenGL ES 3.0/GLSL ES 3.00 format/packing contracts
provide the compatibility path; GLES 3.2 core float support remains eligible.

